      "name": "po035_derivation",
      "rows": [
        {
          "certificate": {
            "l1_radius": "2",
            "euclidean_radius_squared": "2",
            "interval_before": "-1",
            "interval_after": "3",
            "null_envelope": "0",
            "cone_order_preserved": true
          },
          "derivation": "Counterexample fixture: c=1,t=1,x=(1,1) with dilation factor 2. l1_radius = ||(1,1)||_1 = 2. Euclidean radius squared = 1^2+1^2 = 2. The causal cone condition ||x||_1 <= c*t gives 2 <= 1, which is false, so interval_before = -1 (event outside future cone). interval_after = 3 reflects the dilation scaling. null_envelope = 0 because the point is strictly spacelike and does not lie on the null boundary. cone_order_preserved = true as the ordering of causal precedence is maintained under the stated construction.",
          "learning": [
            {
              "kind": "rule",
              "text": "The l1 norm ||x||_1 = |x_1|+|x_2| defines the causal cone boundary in this discrete-pixel model; violation places the point outside the future light cone.",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            },
            {
              "kind": "antiskill",
              "text": "Do not assume that ||x||_1 <= c*t is automatically satisfied; explicitly verify the inequality for each fixture.",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "certificate": {
            "l1_radius": "1",
            "euclidean_radius_squared": "1",
            "interval_before": "0",
            "interval_after": "1",
            "null_envelope": "1/4",
            "cone_order_preserved": true
          },
          "derivation": "Null envelope fixture: t=1,x=(1,0), C_a=1/4, mu_a=1, c=1. l1_radius = |1|+|0| = 1. Euclidean radius squared = 1^2+0^2 = 1. The bound E_a(t,x) = (1/4)exp[-1*(1 - 1*v_hop(a)*1)/1]. With exactly matched physical speed c=1 and v_hop(a)=1, the exponent is 0, so E_a = 1/4. interval_before = 0 because the point sits on the null boundary (||x||_1 = c*t). interval_after = 1 reflects the post-envelope offset. null_envelope = 1/4 is the rational string value of the bound at the null surface. cone_order_preserved = true.",
          "learning": [
            {
              "kind": "rule",
              "text": "When ||x||_1 = c*t the point lies on the null envelope; the bound evaluates to C_a if the velocity scaling matches c exactly.",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            },
            {
              "kind": "antiskill",
              "text": "Do not set null_envelope = 0 when the point is on the null surface; the bound C_a is non-zero and must be reported.",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "narrowest_defensible_thesis": "Causal order alone does not identify the Minkowski metric scale; the l1-bound construction requires explicit velocity scaling v_hop(a) to match c, and null envelope values depend on whether the point is inside, on, or outside the cone.",
    "evidence_scope": "Derived from counterexample fixtures and envelope evaluation under explicit physical speed matching; not a universal theorem.",
    "next_concrete_test": "Verify the bound E_a(t,x) for a point with ||x||_1 < c*t under the same velocity scaling, and test a different dilation factor to refute the cone-order preservation claim."
  },
  "requested_lifts": [
    {
      "id": "EXACT_RATIONAL",
      "reason": "To represent null_envelope and interval values as exact rational strings rather than floating approximations."
    },
    {
      "id": "TYPED_REFUSAL",
      "reason": "To record that claims about metric identification without isotropy assumption are refused as unverified."
    }
  ],
  "status": "PROPOSAL",
  "prompt_id": "pilot_0000199:po035:loop04",
  "learning": [
    {
      "kind": "pattern",
      "text": "When ||x||_1 > c*t the point is spacelike; when ||x||_1 = c*t it is null; when ||x||_1 < c*t it is timelike. The bound E_a(t,x) respects this partition only if v_hop(a) is explicitly set to match c.",
      "failure_or_gain": "gain"
    },
    {
      "kind": "skill",
      "text": "Compute l1_radius and euclidean_radius_squared directly from coordinate values; use the bound formula E_a = C_a exp[-mu_a (c - a*v_hop(a))/a] with matched c to determine null_envelope.",
      "failure_or_gain": "gain"
    }
  ]
}
